{"card":{"card_id":"ma-c-5d678abeb82cb55e4395","statement":"Note that if $H$ is unipotent, then $\\shv((H,\\chi)\\bs X)\\cong\\shv((H,\\hchi)\\bs X)\\subset \\shv(X)$ by virtue of <<ref:ex: monodromic system on unipotent group>>.\n\nHowever, this is not the case in general if $H$ is not unipotent. But as the functor $(\\Mod_\\La)_\\chi\\to \\shv_{\\chi\\mbox{-}\\mon}(H)$ is $\\shv(H)$-linear and the image generates the target, we see that $\\shv((H,\\hchi)\\bs X)$ is generated (as $\\La$-linear category) by the essential image of the functor $\\shv((H,\\chi)\\bs X)\\to \\shv(X)$. On the other hand, using the expression $\\shv((H,\\hchi)\\bs X)\\cong \\shv_{\\chi\\mbox{-}\\mon}(H)\\otimes_{\\shv(H)} \\shv(X)$, we see that $\\shv_{\\chi\\mbox{-}\\mon}(X)$ is generated by $a_*(\\Ch_\\chi\\boxtimes \\mF)$ for $\\Ch_\\chi$ being character sheaves on $H$ and $\\mF\\in \\shv(X)$. Here $a: H\\times X\\to X$ denotes the action map. Therefore, our definition of the category of $(\\chi\\mbox{-})$monodromic sheaves on $X$ coincides with other definition used in literature.","source_id":"arXiv:2504.07482","cluster":"representation_theory","statement_sha256":"627b01a5f13b977b2446da32f10146414e9c8e3b1abc425b361132ca9fd280aa","kind":"remark","label":"Remark 245","ref_key":"rem: equivariant category not subcategory","name":"","order":344,"deps":[{"ref":"ex: monodromic system on unipotent group","card_id":"ma-c-14f40cf261b7e0ed79a0","label":"Example 237","resolved":true,"target":"card"}],"cite_keys":[],"provenance":{"source_url":"https://arxiv.org/abs/2504.07482","harvest_mode":"arxiv_eprint","payload_sha256":"1b700e8c4a2fc6f0c0f522039f223820ba6737a9a0ac91aea37c58ba7a3389c2","line":7397,"origin":"latex_env","retrieved_at":"2026-09-28T11:10:54+08:00"},"wash":{"version":"cardwash.v3","stages":["segment","purify","classify","dedupe","emit"],"numbering":"document_order_with_label_heuristic","detail":{"stripped_proof":false,"chars":960,"math_hints":93}}},"paper":{"source_id":"arXiv:2504.07482","title":"Tame categorical local Langlands correspondence","abstract":"In one of our previous articles, we outlined the formulation of a version of the categorical arithmetic local Langlands conjecture. The aims of this article are threefold. First, we provide a detailed account of one component of this conjecture: the local Langlands category. Second, we aim to prove this conjecture in the tame case for quasi-split unramified reductive groups. Finally, we will explore the first applications of such categorical equivalence.","authors":["Xinwen Zhu"],"year":"2025","url":"https://arxiv.org/abs/2504.07482","cluster":"representation_theory","macros":{"fraka":"{\\mathfrak a}","frakb":"{\\mathfrak b}","frakc":"{\\mathfrak c}","frakg":"{\\mathfrak g}","frakh":"{\\mathfrak h}","frakm":"{\\mathfrak m}","frakp":"{\\mathfrak p}","fraks":"{\\mathfrak s}","frakt":"{\\mathfrak t}","fraku":"{\\mathfrak u}","frakA":"{\\mathfrak A}","frakC":"{\\mathfrak C}","frakM":"{\\mathfrak M}","frakX":"{\\mathfrak X}","bA":"{\\mathbb A}","bB":"{\\mathbb B}","bC":"{\\mathbb C}","bD":"{\\mathbb D}","bF":"{\\mathbb F}","bG":"{\\mathbb G}","bL":"{\\mathbb L}","bN":"{\\mathbb N}","bO":"{\\mathbb O}","bP":"{\\mathbb P}","bQ":"{\\mathbb Q}","bR":"{\\mathbb R}","bT":"{\\mathbb T}","bX":"{\\mathbb X}","bZ":"{\\mathbb Z}","bfA":"{\\mathbf A}","bfB":"{\\mathbf B}","bfC":"{\\mathbf C}","bfD":"{\\mathbf D}","bfE":"{\\mathbf E}","bfF":"{\\mathbf F}","bfG":"{\\mathbf G}","bfH":"{\\mathbf H}","bfI":"{\\mathbf I}","bfK":"{\\mathbf K}","bfL":"{\\mathbf L}","bfM":"{\\mathbf M}","bfN":"{\\mathbf N}","bfP":"{\\mathbf P}","bfR":"{\\mathbf R}","bfS":"{\\mathbf S}","bfT":"{\\mathbf T}","bfa":"{\\mathbf a}","bff":"{\\mathbf f}","mA":"{\\mathcal A}","mB":"{\\mathcal B}","mE":"{\\mathcal E}","mF":"{\\mathcal F}","mG":"{\\mathcal G}","mH":"{\\mathcal H}","mI":"{\\mathcal I}","mJ":"{\\mathcal J}","mK":"{\\mathcal K}","mL":"{\\mathcal L}","mM":"{\\mathcal M}","mN":"{\\mathcal N}","mO":"{\\mathcal O}","mP":"{\\mathcal P